    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it really does feel like a valve. and the more i track it, the more it doesn't feel like a coincidence. like, last tuesday i took a different route to the subway just because the lighting felt off on my usual path, and i ended up bumping into an old colleague who happened to be passing through a crisis with his firm. that one conversation prevented a massive fallout. it's almost like i'm being guided to the specific nodes where the interference is needed most. i'm starting to wonder if there's a way to be more systematic about it. how would one even begin to map out these \"nodes\" of tension so i can be more effective?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
